    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0828" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.154/366: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-20T11:00:00-06:00">November 20, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>94. Referring to Department’s instruction No. 203 of October 15,<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d555-f1"/> the President informs me orally that the Salvadoran
                    Government agrees gladly to the aerial survey.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
